Aerie-Purpose: Ask the user, once for each site, whether to turn on Widevine when a page first uses encrypted media.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/media/key_system_support_impl.cc, content/public/browser/content_browser_client.{h,cc}, chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.{h,cc}, components/infobars/core/infobar_delegate.h, tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/browser/enums.xml, chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
Aerie-Kind: hook

A frame asks the browser for key system support (KeySystemSupportImpl::SetObserver) when
it first uses encrypted media. The new ContentBrowserClient::OnEncryptedMediaRequested()
does nothing by default; ChromeContentBrowserClient forwards it to
chrome/browser/aerie_widevine (overlay), which shows the infobar if Widevine is off and
the user has not declined the site. The infobar has a new identifier.

